Replaces [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) for this review. The old
accepted record is preserved. The [incident review](/kb/incidents/4471-review) shows
why matching subjects merged separate failures into one ticket.

## Decision

Read the body and identify tenant, tenant locale, form version and channel. Merge only
when evidence supports the same failing path. Compare the supplied cause logic with
the symptoms; do not silently override contradictory evidence. Keep unresolved cases
for investigation. Browser locale, intake tag and subject alone cannot establish cause.

Count unique report IDs. Preserve received and merged timestamps independently. Keep
one engineering issue per confirmed problem and link related issues rather than merging
them just because they produce a similar symptom.

## What the running logic already distinguishes

<DedupeExplorer />

The same tenant on app versus email can share a cause despite different subjects.
The same subject and tenant on form versus app can have different causes. Identical
subjects on different tenants' forms can differ by form version. Unknown tenants do
not have an established cause and must not be merged on that basis.

## Consequences

Triage takes more reading and tenant lookup. It keeps a smaller issue from disappearing
inside a larger ticket. New reports continue to arrive: recheck the data and ticket
assignments instead of treating a “known” label as evidence that the failures stopped.

